// Relationship Demo: Social Simulation
// Demonstrates @character, @relationship, and @faction directives

=== start ===
Welcome to the Royal Court!

You are a newly appointed diplomat tasked with navigating the complex web of court politics.

// Register characters
@character id="princess" name="Princess Elena" faction="royals"
@character id="knight" name="Sir Marcus" faction="military"
@character id="merchant" name="Lady Thorne" faction="traders"

// Register factions
@faction id="royals" name="The Royal Family" rep=50
@faction id="military" name="The Knight's Order" rep=0
@faction id="traders" name="The Merchant's Guild" rep=0

Your success depends on building relationships and managing faction reputations.

* [Attend the morning court] -> morning_court

=== morning_court ===
@scene bg="throne_room.jpg" music="royal_theme.mp3"

The throne room is filled with nobles, knights, and merchants.

Princess Elena sits on the throne, presiding over court matters.

* [Approach the Princess] -> meet_princess
* [Speak with Sir Marcus] -> meet_knight
* [Chat with Lady Thorne] -> meet_merchant

=== meet_princess ===
@char name="Princess Elena" portrait="elena_neutral.jpg"

"Ah, our new diplomat!" Princess Elena greets you.

"I trust you'll serve the crown well."

* [Bow respectfully] -> princess_respect
* [Speak casually] -> princess_casual

=== princess_respect ===
@relationship with="princess" affection=+10 respect=+15
@faction id="royals" rep=+10

You bow deeply. "Your Highness, I am honored to serve."

The Princess smiles approvingly.

"I can see you understand proper protocol. We shall get along well."

{$rel.princess.respect > 60}
  "In fact, I have a sensitive diplomatic mission that requires someone I can trust..."
  -> princess_quest
{else}
  "Continue to serve loyally, and you will rise in the court."
  -> court_mingling
{/}

=== princess_casual ===
@relationship with="princess" affection=+5 respect=-5

"Hey, nice to meet you!" you say with a friendly wave.

The Princess raises an eyebrow at your informal manner.

"I... see. Do remember that we maintain certain standards here."

-> court_mingling

=== princess_quest ===
@relationship with="princess" trust=+20

Princess Elena leans in conspiratorially.

"There are tensions between the Knights and the Merchants. I need you to mediate."

"Build bridges between them. The stability of the realm depends on it."

* [Accept the mission] -> diplomatic_mission

=== meet_knight ===
@char name="Sir Marcus" portrait="marcus_armor.jpg"

Sir Marcus stands tall in his gleaming armor.

"You're the new diplomat? Let's see if you're worth your salt."

* [Challenge him to a sparring match] -> knight_spar
* [Ask about his military campaigns] -> knight_talk

=== knight_spar ===
@relationship with="knight" respect=+20 rivalry=+10
@faction id="military" rep=+15

"A sparring match? Bold!" Marcus grins.

You exchange blows in the training yard. Though he clearly holds back, you manage to land a few hits.

"You've got spirit! I respect that."

{$rel.knight.respect > 30}
  "The Order could use someone like you. We have a mission against bandits in the northern pass..."
  -> knight_quest
{else}
  "Keep training. You show promise."
  -> court_mingling
{/}

=== knight_talk ===
@relationship with="knight" friendship=+10
@faction id="military" rep=+5

"Ah, you want to hear war stories?" Marcus's eyes light up.

He regales you with tales of battles and heroism.

You listen attentively, asking thoughtful questions.

-> court_mingling

=== knight_quest ===
"I need a diplomatic envoy to negotiate with the mountain clans."

"They respect strength. If you've earned my trust, you can earn theirs."

* [Accept the mission] -> military_mission

=== meet_merchant ===
@char name="Lady Thorne" portrait="thorne_smile.jpg"

Lady Thorne regards you with calculating eyes.

"A diplomat? Excellent. Perhaps we can do business."

* [Discuss trade agreements] -> merchant_trade
* [Ask about guild politics] -> merchant_politics

=== merchant_trade ===
@relationship with="merchant" trust=+15 affection=+5
@faction id="traders" rep=+10

"Trade is the lifeblood of the kingdom," Lady Thorne explains.

She outlines various commercial opportunities and how diplomacy can facilitate them.

{$rel.merchant.trust > 40}
  "I have a proposal that could benefit both of us greatly..."
  -> merchant_quest
{else}
  "We should speak again when you've proven yourself reliable."
  -> court_mingling
{/}

=== merchant_politics ===
@relationship with="merchant" affection=+10

Lady Thorne leans in, speaking softly.

"The Merchant's Guild has many... interests. And many rivals."

She shares insights into the complex web of trade politics.

-> court_mingling

=== merchant_quest ===
"There's a trade route the Knights have blocked for 'security reasons.'"

"Convince Sir Marcus to reopen it, and the Guild will be in your debt."

* [Accept the mission] -> diplomatic_mission

=== court_mingling ===
You've made some initial connections at court.

{$rel.princess.status == "friend"}
  Princess Elena considers you a trusted ally.
{/}

{$rel.knight.status == "friend"}
  Sir Marcus respects you as a fellow warrior.
{/}

{$rel.merchant.status == "friend"}
  Lady Thorne sees you as a valuable business partner.
{/}

* [Continue diplomatic work] -> diplomatic_mission

=== diplomatic_mission ===
Over the following weeks, you work to balance competing interests:

{$faction.military.standing == "friendly" && $faction.traders.standing == "friendly"}
  You successfully mediate between the Knights and Merchants!

  A compromise is reached: enhanced security on trade routes satisfies both parties.

  @faction id="royals" rep=+25
  @relationship with="princess" trust=+30

  -> diplomatic_success
{else}
  Your diplomatic efforts continue...

  {$faction.military.standing != "friendly"}
    You need to build better relations with the Knight's Order.
  {/}

  {$faction.traders.standing != "friendly"}
    You need to win the trust of the Merchant's Guild.
  {/}

  * [Visit Sir Marcus] -> meet_knight
  * [Visit Lady Thorne] -> meet_merchant
{/}

=== diplomatic_success ===
@scene bg="throne_room.jpg" music="victory.mp3"

Princess Elena addresses the court:

"Our new diplomat has achieved what many thought impossible!"

"Through wisdom and perseverance, the realm is more united than ever."

{$rel.princess.romance > 50}
  She meets your eyes with a warm smile. Something more than professional respect passes between you.

  "Perhaps we should discuss your future role... in private."

  -> romance_ending
{/}

{$rel.princess.status == "close_friend"}
  "You have proven yourself a true friend to the crown. I name you Royal Ambassador!"

  -> success_ending
{/}

-> success_ending

=== romance_ending ===
In the quiet of the palace gardens, Princess Elena takes your hand.

"You've won not just my respect, but my heart."

The future holds not just diplomatic triumphs, but something far more precious.

-> END

=== success_ending ===
Your diplomatic career flourishes.

Through careful relationship building and faction management, you've secured your place in history.

Relationships:
{$rel.princess.status}: Princess Elena
{$rel.knight.status}: Sir Marcus
{$rel.merchant.status}: Lady Thorne

Faction standings:
{$faction.royals.standing}: Royal Family
{$faction.military.standing}: Knight's Order
{$faction.traders.standing}: Merchant's Guild

-> END

=== military_mission ===
// Path focused on military faction
@faction id="military" rep=+20

You embark on the military mission...

// This would branch into military-focused gameplay

-> success_ending

=== END ===
The end of your story... for now.
